{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Science, Old and New"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A New Life"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Organizing Points in an Argument"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Discourse markers show how ideas are connected. They usually come at the beginning of a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discourse markers can show a  <span class=\"strong\">connection</span> to what the speaker is saying and what  was just said. They can also show what the speaker's  <span class=\"strong\">opinion</span> is  about what is being said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some discourse markers include:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Discourse Marker\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" at the time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" After all\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" emphasizing \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"then\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" after that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" so\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" because of this\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" of course\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" as everybody knows, as is obvious\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" in fact\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to emphasize \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" according to him\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" in his words\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" for this reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" introducing a cause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" so that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" giving a purpose\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When Brad lost his leg in that horrific car accident last year, he was devastated. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In fact, he became very depressed and withdrawn."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Of course, we worried that this would be irrevocable. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "After all, Brad had always been athletic and loved sports. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, he was certain that his life, as he knew it, would be over. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Then, your office contacted him and gave him hope. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "According to him, this opportunity changed his life forever. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For this reason, he now views his life in a different light. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In fact, he has decided to go into medicine so that he can help others as you have helped him."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Of course, I cannot thank or praise you enough. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals for Possibility and Certainty "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use must, may, might, and could to describe degrees of certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Must = it's very likely <br/> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br/> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br/> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs.  They come before the dictionary form (infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to</span>) of the main verb.  Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the \"receiver\" of the action, rather than the \"doer\" of the action. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They can use this information. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" active modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They can be used to solve engineering problems.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" passive modal\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Brad worked tirelessly with your team so his new leg could function like his real leg. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He has decided to go into medicine so that he can help others as you have helped him."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We worried that this would be irrevocable. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He was certain that his life, as he knew it, would be over. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They said he could be fitted with a robotic prosthesis. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The prosthesis could be controlled with his mind."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deepest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "most heartfelt"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am writing to express my deepest gratitude for what you have done for our son, Brad."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk someone with a his new prosthesis."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gratitude"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the quality or feeling of being grateful or thankful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We would like to express our gratitude to you, Dr. Richardson."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "horrific"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used for emphasizing how big and shocking something is"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Brad lost his leg in that horrific car accident last year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "irrevocable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to be repealed or annulled"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Of course, we worried that his lost would be irrevocable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be adapted to or suitable for (a purpose, object, occasion, etc.)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They said he could be fitted with a robotic prosthesis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to control"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to dominate or command "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The prosthesis could be controlled with his mind."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob07aud06"}], "type": 